    "goal": "Co-incubate CYP2D6 with UDPGA at 121.2 µM substrate (Km = 198.5 µM) in the presence of a competitive inhibitor (Ki = 201.5 µM) at 218.6 µM, Vmax = 4.8803 µmol/min, to determine the run-condition IC50 and inhibited reaction velocity.",
    "rationale": "Competitive inhibition of CYP2D6-mediated UDPGA conjugation. The run-condition IC50 follows Cheng–Prusoff: IC50 = Ki(1 + [S]/Km) = 201.5 × (1 + 121.2/198.5) ≈ 324.5 µM. The inhibited velocity is Vmax × fractional activity, where fractional activity = [S]/(Km(1+[I]/Ki)+[S]) ≈ 0.2265, giving v ≈ 1.106 µmol/min. Assumes Michaelis–Menten competitive kinetics, saturating UDPGA cofactor, and free (unbound) substrate/inhibitor concentrations.",
